N	Module	"ky.source.types.ResponsePromise"	{"absolute_path":"<root>/source/types/ResponsePromise.ts","docstring":"Returns a `Response` object with `Body` methods added for convenience. So you can, for example, call `ky.get(input).json()` directly without having to await the `Response` first. When called like that, an appropriate `Accept` header will be set depending on the body method used. Unlike the `Body` methods of `window.Fetch`; these will throw an `HTTPError` if the response status is not in the range of `200...299`. Also, `.json()` will return an empty string if body is empty or the response status is `204` instead of throwing a parse error due to an empty body.","flow_covered":false,"interface_fingerprint":"efd2c2085bd1a91be7ddb0370e9c286bb6b799c17c3e343773b7e2d7c6b8b771","name":"ResponsePromise.ts","path":"source/types/ResponsePromise.ts","unresolved_references":[],"unresolved_specifiers":[]}
